            <ArticleTitle>An alternative to costly clinics.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>18-20</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.7748/ns.31.28.18.s22</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>More than 7,200 British women have endometrial cancer diagnosed every year. It is a figure that is rising markedly, with the cancer being linked to problems with obesity on an international scale. Although an early diagnosis leads to a good prognosis, after treatment has been completed patients are asked to attend regular outpatient clinic appointments for three to five years.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
